\solonow plays only the instruments given as arguments and
mutes all others, immediately.
Its syntax is the following:

\solonow \violin \cello

where \violin and \cello are instruments created with
\insts.init. The solo instruments are unmuted, if they
have been muted before.
To play all instruments again, call:

\solonow \all

Unlike \solo, which waits for the start of the next bar,
\solonow takes effect at once, even in the middle of a bar.

Muted instruments show a whole rest in the score and are
hidden in the piano roll.

\solonow needs at least one argument. An argument that is
not an instrument results in an "unknown instrument" error.
